// RIPEMD-160, from the European RIPE project (Dobbertin, Bosselaers, Preneel,
// 1996).
//
// Two parallel lines of eighty rounds, mixed at the end rather than during: the
// design is MD4's compression function run twice with different constants and
// message orders, and the result combined across both lines. That is what makes
// it a different hash rather than a stronger MD4, and it is why the two lines
// cannot be computed separately.
//
// It is legacy. No new protocol should pick it — SHA-2 and SHA-3 are faster on
// every target that matters and have had far more attention — but Bitcoin's
// address format, OpenPGP fingerprints and a long tail of older systems all still
// name it, and a library that cannot compute it cannot interoperate.
import {
  "moonbitstack/mooncrypt/spec",
}

import {
  "moonbitstack/moonbase/base16",
  "moonbitlang/core/encoding/utf8",
} for "test"
